---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv_en">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    Data Science student graduating in September 2026, with a strong foundation in
    <strong>machine learning</strong>, <strong>statistical analysis</strong>, and
    <strong>computer vision</strong>.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="International Master's Degree in Data Science"
      subtitle="2024 – 2026 at École Centrale de Lille & University of Lille, France"
    >
      Jointly organized by <strong>Centrale Lille</strong>, <strong>IMT Nord Europe</strong>,
      and the <strong>University of Lille</strong>.
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science (BUT)"
      subtitle="2021 – 2024 at IUT Amiens, France"
    >
      Specialization in <strong>Data Administration, Management, and Exploitation</strong>.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Data Science Intern at CHU Lille"
      subtitle="March 11 – August 28, 2026 at the Medical Imaging Engineering Team, Lille, France"
    >
      Developed a <strong>U-Net</strong> model to segment retinal layers in
      <strong>OCT images</strong>, including benchmarking against state-of-the-art
      methods, clinical comparison, and deployment of the solution.
      <br />
      → Achieved excellent results with a <strong>Dice score of 0.97</strong>.
      A <strong>scientific publication</strong> based on the work conducted during
      the internship is currently under consideration.
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Machine Learning Intern at IRCICA"
      subtitle="May – August 2025 at IRCICA Research Laboratory, Lille, France"
    >
      Built a <strong>people-counting pipeline</strong> using
      <strong>Vision Transformers (ViT)</strong>, including camera setup,
      image acquisition, data preprocessing, fine-tuning, and evaluation on
      multi-camera datasets.
      <br />
      → Results revealed a <strong>lack of generalization</strong>.
      A larger and more representative dataset would be needed to develop a
      <strong>more robust and reliable model</strong>.
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Machine Learning Intern at Laboratoire des Technologies Innovantes"
      subtitle="March 11 – June 7, 2024 at Laboratoire des Technologies Innovantes, France"
    >
      Developed a <strong>temporal forecasting model</strong> using
      <strong>Gradient-Boosted Trees</strong> to predict the evolution of
      <strong>CO₂ levels</strong> based on room information.
      Created a <strong>time series model</strong>, applied
      <strong>feature engineering</strong>, and measured the impact of each feature.
      <br />
      → Despite limited prior experience in machine learning, successfully developed
      a <strong>robust and reliable model</strong>, highlighting the difficulty of
      handling <strong>shifting patterns</strong>.
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Software Development Intern at Orange Business"
      subtitle="April 11 – June 2, 2023 at Orange Business, France"
    >
      Developed the front end of a web application for
      <strong>translation version centering</strong> using <strong>Vue.js</strong>
      and implemented <strong>unit tests</strong>. Used <strong>Git</strong> and
      <strong>Azure DevOps</strong> in a professional environment.
      <br />
      → A <strong>work-study position</strong> was offered following the internship,
      but I chose to focus on further studies in <strong>Data Science</strong>.
      The final project has since been <strong>launched and is currently used</strong>
      for several products within the company.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div>
      <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">AI & Machine Learning</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6">
        <li><strong>Natural Language Processing:</strong> text classification, embeddings</li>
        <li><strong>Computer Vision:</strong> object detection, image classification</li>
        <li><strong>Models:</strong> BERT, Transformers, CNNs, ResNet</li>
        <li><strong>Frameworks:</strong> PyTorch, TensorFlow, Hugging Face</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Applied Mathematics & Statistics</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6">
        <li>
          <strong>Probability & Optimization:</strong> Markov chain Monte Carlo,
          Bayesian inference, gradient descent
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Machine Learning Theory:</strong> bias-variance trade-off,
          regularization, overfitting
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Data Analysis:</strong> statistics, PCA, clustering
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Technical Skills</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6">
        <li><strong>SQL</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Git</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Azure DevOps</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Agile methodologies</strong></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Languages</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6">
        <li>French — Native</li>
        <li>English — Fluent</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Interests</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10">
    <li>Climbing</li>
    <li>Jazz</li>
    <li>Cooking</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>